WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:03.520
What if just one
lifestyle change

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:06.320
could help you
avoid getting cancer,

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:08.160
or diabetes,
or heart disease,

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:09.600
or high blood pressure?

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:12.880
This one change could cut
your risk of chronic disease

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:14.720
and add years to your life.

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:18.480
Well, the simple solution to
so many of these problems

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:20.800
is to eat a healthy diet.

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:24.160
In other words, one centered
around whole plant foods.

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:27.680
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast,

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:30.160
I'm your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:32.720
Today on the
podcast we look at

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:36.240
the best way to control
osteo and rheumatoid arthritis,

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:38.960
and we start with a
look at what happens

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:44.251
when topical olive oil is pitted
against an ibuprofen type drug.

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:49.280
Fifty million Americans
suffer from arthritis,

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:52.240
and osteoarthritis of the knee
is the most common form,

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:54.160
making it a leading
cause of disability.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:57.520
Several inflammatory pathways
underlie the onset and

00:00:57.520 --> 00:01:00.400
progression of the disease,
and so various anti-inflammatory

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:02.800
foods have been put to the test.

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:05.600
Strawberries decrease the
levels circulating in the blood

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:09.040
of an inflammatory mediator
known as tumor necrosis factor,

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:13.040
but that doesn’t necessarily
translate into clinical improvement.

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:15.920
For example, drinking
cherry juice can lower a sign

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:17.760
of inflammation known
as C-reactive protein,

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:20.240
but it failed to help with the disease.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:24.000
But wait, it says
“provided symptom relief.”

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:29.440
Yeah, it did, but no better than
placebo, meaning drinking it

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:31.680
was essentially no better
than doing nothing.

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:35.680
Cherries may help with another
kind of arthritis called gout,

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:38.560
but they failed when it
came to osteoarthritis.

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:40.640
The same with pomegranate juice.

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:43.840
No significant improvement
in symptoms, but then again,

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:47.280
no significant improvement in
inflammatory mediators either;

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:49.280
so, perhaps there’s no surprise.

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:51.680
But strawberries did
decrease inflammation.

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:55.440
Let’s see if they actually
help in a randomized,

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:57.920
double-blind cross-over trial, and . . .

00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:01.200
dietary strawberries were
indeed found to have a significant

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:04.560
analgesic effect, causing a
significant decrease in pain.

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:10.000
There are tumor necrosis factor
inhibitor drugs on the market

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:15.040
now available for the low, low
cost of only about $40,000 a year.

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:18.640
For that kind of money, you’d want
some really juicy side effects,

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:23.280
and they do not disappoint,
like an especially fatal lymphoma.

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:27.120
I think I’ll stick with the strawberries.

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:31.040
One of the reasons we suspected
berries might help is that

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:33.760
if you give people the
equivalent of either a cup a day

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:36.080
of blueberries, or two
cups a day of strawberries,

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:39.200
and then drip their blood
onto cells in a petri dish,

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:41.760
you can see a significant
blunting of inflammation

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:44.240
compared to those who
got placebo berries.

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:47.440
And note that the attenuation of
inflammation got better with time,

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:49.840
so apparently the longer
you eat berries the better.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:53.440
Are there any other foods
that have been tested in this way?

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:57.280
Researchers in France harvested
cartilage from knee replacement

00:02:57.280 --> 00:03:00.640
surgeries and then exposed
them to concentrates of the blood

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:02.320
of volunteers who
took a whopping dose

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:05.040
of a grapeseed and olive extract.

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:08.000
They saw a significant drop
of induced inflammation.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:10.240
There haven’t been any human
studies putting grapeseeds

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:13.920
to the test for arthritis,
but an olive extract was shown

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:16.640
to decrease pain and
improve daily activities

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:18.640
in osteoarthritis sufferers.

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:22.160
So, does this mean adding olive
oil to one’s diet may help?

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:27.600
No, because they used freeze-
dried olive vegetation water.

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:31.600
That’s basically what’s left
over after you extract the oil

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:34.400
from the olives; it’s all
the water-soluble components.

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:36.400
In other words, it’s all
the stuff that’s in an olive

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:38.080
that‘s missing from olive oil.

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:42.000
If you give people actual olives,
a dozen large green olives a day,

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:46.240
you can see a before versus after
drop in an inflammatory mediator.

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:48.240
What if you look only at the oil?

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:50.800
A systematic review and meta-analysis

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:53.440
on the anti-inﬂammatory
beneﬁts of olive oil

00:03:54.320 --> 00:03:57.440
found there does not appear to be any.

00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:01.360
But wait, what about papers
that ascribe remarkable

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:05.120
anti-inflammatory effects
to extra virgin olive oil?

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:08.400
Here’s their evidence on. . . rodents.

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:13.280
In people, extra virgin olive oil
may be no better than butter

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:16.880
when it comes to inflammation,
and worse than even coconut oil.

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:19.360
So, should we just stick to olives?

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:22.240
Sadly, a dozen olives a day
could take up nearly half

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:24.720
your sodium limit for the entire day.

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:28.960
When put to the test, extra virgin
olive oil did not appear

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:31.600
to help with fibromyalgia
symptoms either,

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:34.160
but it did work better than canola oil

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:37.440
in alleviating symptoms of
inflammatory bowel disease.

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:39.760
Unfortunately, I couldn’t find
any studies putting olive oil

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:42.000
intake to the test for arthritis.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:42.919
But wait, why is this video entitled

00:04:42.919 --> 00:04:43.544
Extra Virgin Olive Oil for Arthritis?

00:04:43.545 --> 00:04:47.760
Because (are you ready for this?)
it appears to work topically.

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:52.160
A double-blind, randomized,
clinical trial of topical

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:55.600
virgin olive oil versus a gel
containing an ibuprofen-type

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:57.840
drug for osteoarthritis of the knee.

00:04:57.840 --> 00:05:00.800
Just a gram of oil, which
would be like less than

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:02.800
a quarter teaspoon, three times a day.

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:06.720
So that would cost less than
three cents a day and… it worked!

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:08.960
Topical olive oil was significantly better

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:10.720
than the drug in reducing pain.

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:13.600
And the study only lasted a
month, so maybe the olive oil

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:16.640
would have continued to work
better and better over time.

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:19.600
What about the effectiveness
of olive oil in controlling

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:21.920
morning inflammatory pain
of fingers and knees

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:23.840
among women with
rheumatoid arthritis?

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:27.120
The researchers went all
out, comparing the use of

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:29.760
extra virgin olive oil, to
just rubbing on nothing,

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:33.360
to rubbing on that
ibuprofen-type gel, and evidently

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:35.520
the decrease in the
disease activity score

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:38.240
in the olive oil group beat out the others.

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:45.040
In our next story, pomegranates
are put to the test for weight loss,

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:49.920
diabetes, COPD, prostate cancer,
osteoarthritis, and rheumatoid arthritis.

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:53.840
In a landmark case that made
it all the way up to the

00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:56.640
U.S. Court of Appeals before
being denied review

00:05:56.640 --> 00:06:00.400
by the Supreme Court, POM Wonderful
(the pomegranate juice company)

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:04.480
vs. Federal Trade Commission, a
panel of judges concluded that

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:07.520
many of POM’s ads made
misleading or false claims

00:06:07.520 --> 00:06:10.960
touting medical studies ostensibly
showing that pomegranate products

00:06:10.960 --> 00:06:13.520
could help treat various ailments,
including heart disease,

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:15.760
prostate cancer, and erectile dysfunction,

00:06:15.760 --> 00:06:18.320
and the First Amendment does not protect

00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:20.720
deceptive and misleading advertisements.

00:06:20.720 --> 00:06:24.400
Striking a blow to its billionaire
owners, the Court ruled

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:27.360
that at least one randomized
clinical trial could be required

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:31.040
to substantiate any claims of
treating or preventing disease.

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:36.000
If you look at the medical literature
on the benefits of pomegranates

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:39.280
in general on the “medicinal effects of pomegranate.”

00:06:39.280 --> 00:06:42.000
But if you dig a little deeper
you see this is based on studies

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:46.240
like this: “antiobesity effects
of pomegranate leaf extract

00:06:46.240 --> 00:06:47.840
in a mouse model.”

00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:51.280
First of all, who eats pomegranate leaves?

00:06:51.280 --> 00:06:53.440
And second of all, who’s a mouse?

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:58.720
And if you do have a fat pet mouse,
maybe just feed them less lard.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:02.880
Does pomegranate consumption
affect weight in humans?

00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:05.360
If you look at all the
randomized controlled clinical trials

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:09.920
(meaning human trials), pomegranates
have no significant effect

00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:13.920
on body weight, BMI, belly fat,
or even body fat percentage

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:16.880
in those randomized to
pomegranate product consumption.

00:07:17.920 --> 00:07:21.760
What about for the prevention and
treatment of cardiovascular diseases?

00:07:21.760 --> 00:07:25.760
Researchers reviewed 25 clinical
trials, looking at cholesterol,

00:07:25.760 --> 00:07:29.120
blood pressure, artery function,
atherosclerotic plaque formation,

00:07:29.120 --> 00:07:33.280
and platelet function, and...
even in the best studies,

00:07:33.280 --> 00:07:37.040
they did not find significant
indications of benefit.

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:40.560
Here’s a study on pomegranate
juice and erectile dysfunction.

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:45.360
It was funded by the POM company,
and yet it failed as well.

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:49.040
No benefit for diabetes
markers and no benefit

00:07:49.040 --> 00:07:52.400
for chronic obstructive pulmonary
diseases like emphysema.

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:55.360
They were banking on the antioxidant
activity of pomegranate juice

00:07:55.360 --> 00:07:58.560
to help, but that’s antioxidant activity in vitro

00:07:58.560 --> 00:08:00.800
(meaning in a test tube or petri dish).

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:05.360
To my surprise, a meta-analysis
of data from 11 randomized

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:09.040
controlled trials did not
support convincing evidence

00:08:09.040 --> 00:08:11.920
of pomegranate intake having a
significant increasing effect

00:08:11.920 --> 00:08:14.640
on total antioxidant
capacity of your bloodstream

00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:16.720
because some of the
most potent antioxidants

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:19.840
don’t even seem to be
absorbed into the human body.

00:08:19.840 --> 00:08:22.880
No wonder pomegranate supplementation
didn’t seem to affect

00:08:22.880 --> 00:08:24.720
oxidative stress in tissue samples

00:08:24.720 --> 00:08:26.880
taken from prostate cancer patients.

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:29.280
But, of course, what we care about is whether

00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:31.360
it affects the cancer Itself.

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:36.000
The strongest evidence for the
anticancer activity of pomegranates

00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:38.400
is said to come from
studies on prostate cancer.

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:42.080
Unfortunately, early promising
results were not conﬁrmed

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:43.680
when they were actually put to the test.

00:08:43.680 --> 00:08:46.800
For example, daily pomegranate intake
was found in a randomized

00:08:46.800 --> 00:08:50.160
controlled trial to have
no impact on PSA levels,

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:51.520
a marker of tumor progression.

00:08:51.520 --> 00:08:55.040
And, indeed, a randomized, double-blind,
placebo-controlled trial

00:08:55.040 --> 00:08:57.120
found essentially no
difference when it came to

00:08:57.120 --> 00:08:59.120
prostate cancer disease progression.

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:03.360
They were banking on the anti-
inflammatory activity of

00:09:03.360 --> 00:09:05.040
pomegranate juice to help, but again,

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:07.680
that had been demonstrated in vitro.

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:11.600
In people, a meta-analysis based
on five randomized controlled trials

00:09:11.600 --> 00:09:15.840
published in 2016 concluded
that pomegranate juice did not

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:18.800
have a significant effect on
C-reactive protein levels,

00:09:18.800 --> 00:09:20.480
a key marker of inflammation.

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:23.120
If you look at the forest
plot, though, you’ll see

00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:27.360
all five trials tended towards
lower C-reactive protein levels

00:09:27.360 --> 00:09:31.760
such that the data combined almost
reached statistical significance.

00:09:31.760 --> 00:09:35.040
And indeed, an updated meta-
analysis published in 2020

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:38.160
based on seven studies
did indeed get tipped over into

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:40.400
significance and found a significant drop

00:09:40.400 --> 00:09:43.040
in two other inflammatory markers as well.

00:09:43.040 --> 00:09:46.480
Huh, okay. Well, maybe
pomegranate juice could help

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:49.840
in the control of inﬂammatory
diseases after all.

00:09:49.840 --> 00:09:54.240
But you don’t know...until you put it to the test.

00:09:54.960 --> 00:09:58.800
Osteoarthritis involves the degeneration
of the cushioning cartilage

00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:00.880
within joints, particularly the knees.

00:10:00.880 --> 00:10:03.920
If you take some human
osteoarthritic cartilage samples

00:10:03.920 --> 00:10:06.160
and drip on a pomegranate extract,

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:08.480
you can show cartilage-protective effects.

00:10:08.480 --> 00:10:09.200
Here’s how much cartilage disintegration
was happening at baseline.

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:12.480
Add some inflammation and
cartilage breakdown triples,

00:10:13.280 --> 00:10:17.360
but then add more and more
of this pomegranate extract,

00:10:17.360 --> 00:10:20.480
and you can calm things down.
But again, that’s in a petri dish.

00:10:21.280 --> 00:10:23.520
How do we know that when
we eat pomegranates,

00:10:23.520 --> 00:10:25.520
the active components actually
get into our bloodstream

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:27.200
so they can find their way into our joints?

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:30.880
Cartilage-protecting components
were found to be bioavailable

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:35.440
(at least in rabbits), raising the
possibility that pomegranates

00:10:35.440 --> 00:10:39.120
could be a safe and non-toxic
treatment with no side effects,

00:10:39.120 --> 00:10:42.400
as opposed to the drugs currently
in use. But is it effective?

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:46.800
Clinical trials are in progress,
and so many questions

00:10:46.800 --> 00:10:49.360
will be answered...right now!

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:52.240
The first and only clinical trial to date

00:10:52.240 --> 00:10:54.560
on pomegranate juice and osteoarthritis.

00:10:54.560 --> 00:10:58.400
It’s not a placebo-controlled trial,
but instead randomized people

00:10:58.400 --> 00:11:01.200
to pomegranate juice or nothing at all.

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:04.720
Those drinking the juice did report
less stiffness and impairment

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:07.440
of physical function, but
not significantly better

00:11:07.440 --> 00:11:11.040
than just doing nothing. Shoot.

00:11:11.600 --> 00:11:17.680
But just as I was about to give up
on pomegranates, I saw this study:

00:11:17.680 --> 00:11:20.720
Consumption of a pomegranate
extract suppresses joint damage

00:11:20.720 --> 00:11:26.080
in rheumatoid arthritis. But no...
it was just the POM

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:29.280
‘Not-So-Wonderful’ company
inducing joint damage in a mouse

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:32.880
as a model of rheumatoid
arthritis. Come on!

00:11:33.760 --> 00:11:36.560
What about this open-labeled study,
where the patients knew

00:11:36.560 --> 00:11:37.680
what they were getting?

00:11:37.680 --> 00:11:40.000
Eight people with active
rheumatoid arthritis took some

00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:42.720
pomegranate extract every day,
and the six who stuck with it

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:44.240
reported fewer tender joints.

00:11:45.120 --> 00:11:47.200
But as we learned from
the osteoarthritis study,

00:11:47.200 --> 00:11:50.240
if you don’t have a control group you
have no sense at all of what role,

00:11:50.240 --> 00:11:52.240
if any, the treatment actually plays.

00:11:52.800 --> 00:11:57.840
So finally, we come to this:
a randomized, double-blind,

00:11:57.840 --> 00:12:01.040
placebo-controlled trial. It’s about time!

00:12:01.040 --> 00:12:04.240
Half of the subjects unknowingly
got some pomegranate extracts;

00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:07.440
the other half unknowingly got the
equivalent of a sugar pill and...

00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:10.800
significant improvement in
the number of swollen joints,

00:12:10.800 --> 00:12:14.160
tender joints, pain intensity,
a disease activity score,

00:12:14.160 --> 00:12:16.640
a health assessment questionnaire,
and morning stiffness

00:12:16.640 --> 00:12:19.680
compared to placebo. So, if you
have rheumatoid arthritis,

00:12:19.680 --> 00:12:22.800
I would indeed recommend you
start eating pomegranates.

00:12:22.800 --> 00:12:25.680
Why not just pop pomegranate pills?

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:27.520
After all, it was a pomegranate extract

00:12:27.520 --> 00:12:29.440
that alleviated disease activity.

00:12:30.240 --> 00:12:33.920
One good reason to stick to the
fruit is that when 19 pomegranate

00:12:33.920 --> 00:12:36.480
supplements were actually tested in a laboratory,

00:12:36.480 --> 00:12:41.280
most didn’t actually appear to have
any pomegranate in them at all!

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:45.073
Only 6 out of 19 appeared
to be authentic.

00:12:46.160 --> 00:12:48.960
We would love it if you could
share with us your stories

00:12:48.960 --> 00:12:51.840
about reinventing your health
through evidence-based nutrition.

00:12:52.720 --> 00:12:56.000
Go to nutritionfacts.org/testimonials.

00:12:56.000 --> 00:13:00.240
We may share it on our social
media to help inspire others.

00:13:01.200 --> 00:13:05.440
To see any graphs, charts, graphics,
images, or studies mentioned here,

00:13:05.440 --> 00:13:08.640
please go to the Nutrition Facts Podcast
landing page.

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:11.160
There you’ll find all the
detailed information you need –

00:13:11.160 --> 00:13:15.280
plus, links to all of the sources
we cite to each of these topics.

00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:20.240
My latest two books are
“How to Survive a Pandemic”,

00:13:20.800 --> 00:13:24.000
available on e-book, audiobook,
or actual book.

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:28.080
And the “How Not to Diet Cookbook”,
with more than 100 recipes for

00:13:28.080 --> 00:13:30.240
delicious and nutritious meals.

